      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hemlock bark tanning powered by local streams was the town’s first industry, with about a dozen facilities by the mid‑1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Hudson%2C_New_York",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Frontier Town, a Wild West‑themed amusement park, operated from 1952 to 1998 before reopening in 2018 as a campground and day‑use area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
